gpu.amd.integrated (k250: Config accessor gpu_amd_integrated, default false) has to reach the Rexfile on every join path, through the same channel gpu.toolkit uses (k223, commit 1c60db5):
- OCP::Cmd::Apply::CR writes spec.gpu.amd.integrated onto the OCPNodeProvider CR
- share/robocop/crds/ocpnodeprovider.yaml declares the field
- OCP::Provider->gpu_flags_from_cr reads it back (gpu_amd_integrated 0/1, absent stays absent)
- OCP::Node attribute gpu_amd_integrated (k250 prepares it, ORed with spec.gpu true) -> Rex param gpu_amd_integrated
- OCP::Cmd::Apply::Bootstrap (control planes from ocp.yaml) and OCP::Cmd::Node::Add (CLI join) pass it on
- OCP::Rex lets the param through, if it filters

Why: the integrated gate (spec docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-31-amd-gpu-worker-design.md §1) hands AMD iGPUs/APUs to install_driver only on opt-in. Per node, `ocp node add --gpu` already does that (k250). Cluster-wide (pools, control planes) only this card does.

Lanes: apply (CR.pm, Bootstrap, Add), provider (Provider.pm, Rex.pm), state (Node.pm), infra (CRD). They run one after another, because all of them touch the same params channel. Tests on the model of t/223-gpu-toolkit-cdi.t.
Needs k249 and k250 (Rexfile reads the param, Config accessor exists).

Found under k271 (2026-10-31): when the Rexfile's install_amd skips an integrated GPU, its message tells the user to 'set gpu.amd.integrated: true' — a setting that reaches no node today. The Rexfile, OCP::Config and the AMD design spec make the same claim in comments. This card either wires the setting through, or the advice and the comments get dropped/rewritten to name 'ocp node add --gpu' as the only path until it is.

